## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project following the official documentation.

### Changes Made

**Created:**
- `package-lock.json` - NPM lockfile (project originally had yarn.lock, but npm was used due to environment constraints)

**Modified:**
- `package.json` - Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 as a dependency
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Imported and added the Analytics component from '@vercel/analytics/next'

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the framework-specific instructions for Next.js App Router:

1. **Package Installation**: Installed `@vercel/analytics` using npm with the `--legacy-peer-deps` flag
2. **Component Integration**: Added the `<Analytics />` component to the root layout at `src/app/layout.tsx`
   - Imported: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
   - Placed the component at the end of the `<body>` tag, following the documentation's recommended pattern
3. **Code Preservation**: Maintained all existing code structure, imports, and functionality

### Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ ESLint passed with no errors (only 2 pre-existing warnings unrelated to this change)
- ✅ TypeScript compilation successful
- ✅ All 9 routes generated correctly in production build

### Next Steps

To enable Web Analytics on Vercel:
1. Deploy this application to Vercel
2. Go to your project dashboard on Vercel
3. Navigate to the Analytics tab in the sidebar
4. Click the "Enable" button to activate Web Analytics
5. After enabling and redeploying, analytics data will start being collected

The Analytics component will automatically track page views and web vitals metrics once enabled on Vercel's dashboard.
